From ee99498bfb16607ce03123e703d3cde2074ebe14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 15:52:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 109/206] feat(shorebird): analyze_snapshot self_hash +
 op_subgraph_hash, 1380/1380

Solves SubgraphHasher's per-instruction classifier, which task 58 left at
1185/1380 for self_hash and 842/1380 for op_subgraph_hash. Both now reproduce
all 1380 of Shorebird's own values on their base.so, as digests, and
op_subgraph_hash comes out of the deliberate-absence list.

Transcribed from their AccumulateRecursive (0x100196694); addresses and the
negative controls are in SUBGRAPH_CLASSIFIER_RECON.md. The four changes, by
size of effect on self_hash:

  * the pool and field ordinals count REFERENCES, not distinct indices --
    0x100196c28 pushes onto the walk-global vector unconditionally and only
    then try_emplaces size-1 (1212 -> 1350). The external-target map at +0x128
    genuinely does store map.size(), so the two rules had to be read
    separately.
  * the field-table gate is (w & 0x0A3FFBE0) == 0x08003B40, which pins Rn to
    THR and imm12 to {0x0e,0x0f} -- THR+0x70, field_table_values_ -- not any
    ldr [THR,#x] (1350 -> 1379).
  * the dispatch-table head is 3, 4 or 5 instructions (1379 -> 1380).
  * the classifier looks backwards from the load and pops the entries already
    emitted for the address-forming instructions, then skips 3-n forward, so a
    pool access owns exactly kObjectPoolLoadStoreMinInstructionCount words.

Of the three arms task 58 named, only the x16 pair form is exercised by either
corpus; the movz/movk arm and the Instr::ImmLogical arm have zero coverage and
are implemented because they are in their code, not because anything checks
them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

